  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Free play or two touches",
  "description": "Seven against seven with goalkeepers on about 55 × 40 metres. Play mostly free, but now and then the coach calls \"two!\" – then two touches is the limit until the coach calls \"free!\" again. With two touches the players have to find quick solutions with few touches. When play is free there are more ways to solve the same situation, such as running with the ball or taking a player on.\n\nThe coach does not instruct during play but lets the players solve what happens on their own. Instead, stop the game about every four minutes and ask: which solution did you choose, and what did you see that made you choose it? Let the players answer in their own words.\n\nVariation: play offside now and then, if the team does in matches. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up before the ball arrives – then you have time to choose."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "With two touches: set up your next pass with the first touch."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "When play is free: dare to run with the ball and take players on if there is space ahead."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Off the ball: give the player on the ball both a short and a deep option."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
